"""Tamil Nadu State Board (Samacheer Kalvi) Class 11 and 12 syllabus mapped to JEE Main 2026 and NEET UG 2026: data behind /tn-board-12-analytics.

Matriculation schools in Tamil Nadu have followed the common State Board (HSC) syllabus and textbooks since the Uniform System of School Education, so "TN Matriculation Board" here means the
TN State Board HSC syllabus, examined by the Directorate of Government Examinations (DGE).

Status codes for an entrance-exam chapter against the TN syllabus:
  '12'  taught in the TN Class 12 textbook, so it is examined in the +2 board exam
  '11'  taught in the TN Class 11 textbook (+1 public exam), not in the +2 board exam
  'P'   only partly in TN: some sub-topics are missing, listed in the note
  'N'   not in the TN Class 11 or 12 syllabus: a full gap

JEE chapters, question counts and Tiers come from app/data/jee_syllabus_2026.json (all 19 JEE Main 2026 shifts, our tagging). NEET question counts are indicative averages per paper from
the NEET UG 2022 to 2026 papers (our reading, rounded), for the NMC 2024 syllabus that NEET 2025 and 2026 followed. Confirm the current syllabus in the official bulletins.
"""

